 water and electricity charges for administrative purposes; (v) depreciation and amortization expenses relating to our property, plant and equipment and leased properties used for administrative purposes; and (vi) others, which primarily include bad debt expenses, traveling, repair and maintenance, recruitment expenses, and other miscellaneous expenses for administrative purposes.","context":"General and administrative expenses","section":"Key Components of Results of Operations","block":52,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-100379","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001868395","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868395/000121390026100379/ea030525301ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d.bin","sha256":"28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d"}},{"id":"9a0b5972068925ad70dd02dfd9fa2ada6ad34405fe884972f24b21b1673b724e","quote":"Research and development expenses primarily include: (i) share-based compensation expenses; (ii) costs for procuring materials for research and development activities; (iii) salaries and benefits for research and development personnel; (iv) depreciation, which represents depreciation expenses for property, plant and equipment used for research and development purposes; (v) patent registration-related expenses and patent litigation expenses; and (vi) others, which primarily include consumables, traveling expenses, utilities and miscellaneous expenses.","context":"Research and development expenses","section":"Key Components of Results of Operations","block":54,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-100379","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001868395","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868395/000121390026100379/ea030525301ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d.bin","sha256":"28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d"}},{"id":"ae050dc050d27d8b6627ae8b3425fd6471cabd16fd77bd443e2da15b6b34f34b","quote":"Other income primarily consists of: (i) other non-operating income, inclusive of income from warehouse services, and sales of scrap materials, which represent sales of excess miscellaneous materials left over from our production; (ii) foreign exchange gain or loss arising from currency exchange among U.S. Dollar (“US$”), Euro (“EUR”), Hong Kong Dollar, Renminbi (“RMB”) and Great British Pound; (iii) interest expense on short-term bank borrowings, and interest expense on lease liabilities, which is non-cash and calculated as the difference between lease payments and the net present value of the lease payments over the entire term of the lease.","context":"Other income","section":"Key Components of Results of Operations","block":56,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-100379","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001868395","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868395/000121390026100379/ea030525301ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d.bin","sha256":"28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d"}},{"id":"66162a7e2cc186389b337b7f789247b52a5ab8f07367dc039bb076ec70980106","quote":"The Cayman Islands and the British Virgin Islands (the “BVI”)","context":"Income tax expenses","section":"Key Components of Results of Operations","block":58,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-100379","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001868395","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868395/000121390026100379/ea030525301ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d.bin","sha256":"28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d"}},{"id":"5212e3a3754d6f92001d1f481afcbf7eb99715aaa3bc733948d9e80864c614d2","quote":"We were incorporated in the Cayman Islands and several of our wholly owned subsidiaries were incorporated in the BVI. Under the current laws of the Cayman Islands and the BVI, these entities are not subject to income or capital gains taxes. In addition, dividend payments are not subject to withholding tax in the Cayman Islands and the BVI.","context":"The Cayman Islands and the British Virgin Islands (the “BVI”)","section":"Key Components of Results of Operations","block":59,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-100379","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001868395","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868395/000121390026100379/ea030525301ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d.bin","sha256":"28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d"}},{"id":"9643d6e373b12d97bbb206d9fb82ccf89b4183fac907719c3ac85c909c7ee73b","quote":"According to the Tax (Amendment) (No. 3) Ordinance 2018 published by the Hong Kong government, effective April 1, 2018, under the two-tiered profits tax rates regime, the profits tax rate for the first HKD2 million of assessable profits has been lowered to 8.25% (half of the rate specified in Schedule 8 to the Inland Revenue Ordinance (“IRO”)) for corporations. We were not subject to Hong Kong profit tax for any period presented as we did not have assessable profits during the periods presented.","context":"Hong Kong","section":"Key Components of Results of Operations","block":61,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-100379","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001868395","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868395/000121390026100379/ea030525301ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d.bin","sha256":"28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d"}},{"id":"11111c05e41e1f7e6ddf7ddbdabe13596a919a434f6ee0ebfb72f684618bb2b8","quote":"On December 22, 2017, the U.S. enacted the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act of 2017 (the “Tax Act”), which significantly changed previous U.S. tax laws, including a reduction of corporate income tax rate from 35% to 21% and a one-time transition tax on deemed repatriation of undistributed foreign earnings.","context":"United States","section":"Key Components of Results of Operations","block":64,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-100379","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001868395","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868395/000121390026100379/ea030525301ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d.bin","sha256":"28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d"}},{"id":"66537086895f3218ee5c895ce51ad15e6173ab3a60756d62f8d282f863911876","quote":"Our subsidiaries that were incorporated in EU countries, such as the Netherlands, Italy, and France, are subject to enterprise income tax on the respective country’s taxable income as determined under the tax laws and accounting standards at rates ranging from 16.5% to 28%.","context":"Europe","section":"Key Components of Results of Operations","block":66,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-100379","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001868395","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868395/000121390026100379/ea030525301ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d.bin","sha256":"28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d"}},{"id":"ed06b5cb546e00d4d11d8156930353c65553e0bdfbcea57cfb9873940ccfda43","quote":"Generally, our Mainland PRC subsidiaries are subject to enterprise income tax on their taxable income in China at a statutory rate of 25%, except for certain of our Mainland PRC subsidiaries that are qualified as high and new technology enterprises under the PRC Enterprise Income Tax Law and are eligible for a preferential enterprise income tax rate of 15%. The enterprise income tax is calculated based on the entity’s global income as determined under Mainland PRC tax laws and accounting standards.","context":"Mainland PRC","section":"Key Components of Results of Operations","block":68,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-100379","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001868395","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868395/000121390026100379/ea030525301ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d.bin","sha256":"28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d"}},{"id":"d2f1d88ddd23d82d7e7cd35c829efb5aaf08348f89c8886bf9f0555e2b5498d7","quote":"Our products are primarily subject to value-added tax at a rate of 13% on sales of compatible toner cartridges, in each case less any deductible value-added tax we have already paid or borne. We are also subject to surcharges on value-added tax payments in accordance with Mainland PRC law.","context":"Generally, our Mainland PRC subsidiaries are subject to enterprise income tax on their taxable income in China at a statutory rate of 25%, except for certain of our Mainland PRC subsidiaries that are qualified as high and new technology enterprises under the PRC Enterprise Income Tax Law and are eligible for a preferential enterprise income tax rate of 15%. The enterprise income tax is calculated based on the entity’s global income as determined under Mainland PRC tax laws and accounting standards.","section":"Key Components of Results of Operations","block":69,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-100379","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001868395","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868395/000121390026100379/ea030525301ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d.bin","sha256":"28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d"}},{"id":"6096c902f487dcb1ad5a370f7d8623e01780a07de36770902fc7411af52786f3","quote":"Dividends paid by our Mainland PRC subsidiaries in Mainland China to our Hong Kong subsidiaries will be subject to a withholding tax rate of 10%, unless the relevant Hong Kong entity satisfies all the requirements under the Double Taxation Avoidance Arrangement and receives approval from the relevant tax authority. If our Hong Kong subsidiaries satisfy all the requirements under the tax arrangement and receive approval from the relevant tax authority, then the dividends paid to the Hong Kong subsidiaries would be subject to withholding tax at the standard rate of 5%. Effective from November 1, 2015, the above-mentioned approval requirement has been abolished, but a Hong Kong entity is still required to file an application package with the relevant tax authority, and settle the overdue taxes if the preferential 5% tax rate is denied based on the subsequent review of the application package by the relevant tax authority.","context":"Our products are primarily subject to value-added tax at a rate of 13% on sales of compatible toner cartridges, in each case less any deductible value-added tax we have already paid or borne. We are also subject to surcharges on value-added tax payments in accordance with Mainland PRC law.","section":"Key Components of Results of Operations","block":70,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-100379","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001868395","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868395/000121390026100379/ea030525301ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d.bin","sha256":"28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d"}},{"id":"f4c8fa8a193e30754afa4c39e657c4c38dcc6d131c01b77a81d02acb6a8f3b80","quote":"If we or any of our subsidiaries outside of Mainland China were deemed to be a “resident enterprise” under the PRC Enterprise Income Tax Law, such entity would be subject to enterprise income tax on its worldwide income at a rate of 25%.","context":"Dividends paid by our Mainland PRC subsidiaries in Mainland China to our Hong Kong subsidiaries will be subject to a withholding tax rate of 10%, unless the relevant Hong Kong entity satisfies all the requirements under the Double Taxation Avoidance Arrangement and receives approval from the relevant tax authority. If our Hong Kong subsidiaries satisfy all the requirements under the tax arrangement and receive approval from the relevant tax authority, then the dividends paid to the Hong Kong subsidiaries would be subject to withholding tax at the standard rate of 5%. Effective from November 1, 2015, the above-mentioned approval requirement has been abolished, but a Hong Kong entity is still required to file an application package with the relevant tax authority, and settle the overdue taxes if the preferential 5% tax rate is denied based on the subsequent review of the application package by the relevant tax authority.","section":"Key Components of Results of Operations","block":71,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-100379","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001868395","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868395/000121390026100379/ea030525301ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d.bin","sha256":"28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d"}},{"id":"a3d783bd32edc2462147175d7de9152b645050027cc53905e7f0ab973caeb0c4","quote":"Under the PRC Enterprise Income Tax Law and the Notice on Improvements to Policies of Weighted Pre-tax Deduction of Research and Development Expenses, research and development expenses incurred by an enterprise in the course of carrying out research and development activities that have not formed intangible assets and are included in the profit and loss account for the current year are eligible for additional pre-tax deduction. Starting from January 1, 2021, besides deducting the actual amount of research and development expenses incurred, an enterprise is allowed an additional 100% deduction of such amount in calculating its taxable income for the relevant year, the rate of which was 75% before 2021. For research and development expenses that have formed intangible assets, the tax amortization is based on 200% of the costs of the intangible assets.","context":"If we or any of our subsidiaries outside of Mainland China were deemed to be a “resident enterprise” under the PRC Enterprise Income Tax Law, such entity would be subject to enterprise income tax on its worldwide income at a rate of 25%.","section":"Key Components of Results of Operations","block":72,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-100379","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001868395","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868395/000121390026100379/ea030525301ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d.bin","sha256":"28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d"}},{"id":"38e771dc10b253d6912c4dea9b9c4fcf4176d0b7ed38dd38ea91278e711ef6d3","quote":"In accordance with the implementation rules of the PRC Enterprise Income Tax Law (the “EIT Law”), a qualified “High and New Technology Enterprise” (“HNTE”) is eligible for a preferential tax rate of 15%. The HNTE certificate is effective for a period of three years, and an entity may re-apply for the HNTE certificate upon expiration of the prior certificate. Jiangxi Yibo E-Tech Co., Ltd., a subsidiary of the Company, has been recognized as an HNTE and renewed its HNTE certificate in 2025, which will expire on October 29, 2028. Accordingly, for the six months ended June 30, 2025 and 2026, Jiangxi Yibo E-Tech Co., Ltd. was eligible to enjoy a preferential tax rate of 15% under the EIT Law.","context":"Under the PRC Enterprise Income Tax Law and the Notice on Improvements to Policies of Weighted Pre-tax Deduction of Research and Development Expenses, research and development expenses incurred by an enterprise in the course of carrying out research and development activities that have not formed intangible assets and are included in the profit and loss account for the current year are eligible for additional pre-tax deduction. Starting from January 1, 2021, besides deducting the actual amount of research and development expenses incurred, an enterprise is allowed an additional 100% deduction of such amount in calculating its taxable income for the relevant year, the rate of which was 75% before 2021. For research and development expenses that have formed intangible assets, the tax amortization is based on 200% of the costs of the intangible assets.","section":"Key Components of Results of Operations","block":73,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-100379","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001868395","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868395/000121390026100379/ea030525301ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d.bin","sha256":"28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d"}},{"id":"7d2e0380d7d66d8aba5ade05c9f3b94d38fa50aa9f631a2ef7156f498d8d9632","quote":"For our offline sales to dealers, we mainly sell white-label products and self-branded products through our offline channels. Our revenue from offline sales to dealers decreased by 43.7%, from US$39.4 million for the six months ended June 30, 2025 to US$22.2 million for the six months ended June 30, 2026, mainly due to a decrease in market demand resulting from the imposition of higher U.S. tariffs.","context":"Comparison by Sales Channel","section":"Comparison of Results of Operations for the Six Months Ended June 30, 2025 and 2026","block":78,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-100379","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001868395","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868395/000121390026100379/ea030525301ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d.bin","sha256":"28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d"}},{"id":"22f67ccb6d1ed19cd69cbc0be9f753ba4338de5338b30d6960a3e95be026a620","quote":"For our direct offline sales to ODM customers, our revenue increased by 68.8%, from US$27.7 million for the six months ended June 30, 2025 to US$46.8 million for the six months ended June 30, 2026, which was primarily driven by a significant surge in order volumes resulting from our strategy of offering flexible packaging and pricing options to meet diverse customer requirements.","context":"For our offline sales to dealers, we mainly sell white-label products and self-branded products through our offline channels. Our revenue from offline sales to dealers decreased by 43.7%, from US$39.4 million for the six months ended June 30, 2025 to US$22.2 million for the six months ended June 30, 2026, mainly due to a decrease in market demand resulting from the imposition of higher U.S. tariffs.","section":"Comparison of Results of Operations for the Six Months Ended June 30, 2025 and 2026","block":79,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-100379","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001868395","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868395/000121390026100379/ea030525301ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d.bin","sha256":"28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d"}},{"id":"0b0ecfea3f35664ef2a0cac629bc5deb2f30c31c4a85fe7cc4748f3e165f8704","quote":"For our online sales, we mainly sell self-branded and household products through the Online Selling Platforms. Our revenue generated from online sales decreased by 96.2%, from US$7.4 million for the six months ended June 30, 2025 to US$0.3 million for the six months ended June 30, 2026, mainly due to the completion of our disposal of the online business in December 2025. Following the disposal, we operated only one remaining online store as of June 30, 2026, which conducted clearance sales during the period. We expect to complete the clearance of its remaining inventory by September 2026, after which its operations will cease entirely.","context":"For our direct offline sales to ODM customers, our revenue increased by 68.8%, from US$27.7 million for the six months ended June 30, 2025 to US$46.8 million for the six months ended June 30, 2026, which was primarily driven by a significant surge in order volumes resulting from our strategy of offering flexible packaging and pricing options to meet diverse customer requirements.","section":"Comparison of Results of Operations for the Six Months Ended June 30, 2025 and 2026","block":80,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-100379","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001868395","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868395/000121390026100379/ea030525301ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d.bin","sha256":"28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d"}},{"id":"ecf24731b3a7713ae8b813c0702848ef479ee143323345ce40b404e5d9e90d96","quote":"Our revenue generated from North America decreased by 28.7%, from US$45.3 million for the six months ended June 30, 2025 to US$32.3 million for the six months ended June 30, 2026, due to a decrease in market demand resulting from the imposition of higher U.S. tariffs.","context":"Comparison by Area","section":"Comparison of Results of Operations for the Six Months Ended June 30, 2025 and 2026","block":82,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-100379","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001868395","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868395/000121390026100379/ea030525301ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d.bin","sha256":"28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d"}},{"id":"7aca5fa27dd268c2678b1a8e9ced2069d1facfd521317d5c2faec9f725983807","quote":"Our revenue generated from Europe increased by 23.5%, from US$22.3 million for the six months ended June 30, 2025 to US$27.5 million for the six months ended June 30, 2026, primarily attributable to increased sales volumes resulting from our continuous market expansion efforts in the English and Dutch markets.","context":"Our revenue generated from North America decreased by 28.7%, from US$45.3 million for the six months ended June 30, 2025 to US$32.3 million for the six months ended June 30, 2026, due to a decrease in market demand resulting from the imposition of higher U.S. tariffs.","section":"Comparison of Results of Operations for the Six Months Ended June 30, 2025 and 2026","block":83,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-100379","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001868395","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868395/000121390026100379/ea030525301ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d.bin","sha256":"28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d"}},{"id":"eb3b6f6a098b2bcfe42a60c9390d8f763a03f7c9c8d1e7cd872e821cec09fea9","quote":"Our revenue generated from Asia increased by US$3.1 million, or 53.5%, from US$5.7 million for the six months ended June 30, 2025 to US$8.8 million for the six months ended June 30, 2026, primarily due to our market expansion in China.","context":"Our revenue generated from Europe increased by 23.5%, from US$22.3 million for the six months ended June 30, 2025 to US$27.5 million for the six months ended June 30, 2026, primarily attributable to increased sales volumes resulting from our continuous market expansion efforts in the English and Dutch markets.","section":"Comparison of Results of Operations for the Six Months Ended June 30, 2025 and 2026","block":84,"table":null,"attribution":"managemen