ich was offset by an increase in material costs of US$5.8 million driven by rising prices of raw materials, especially semiconductors and chips.","context":"Cost of revenue","section":"Comparison of Results of Operations for the Six Months Ended June 30, 2025 and 2026","block":87,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-100379","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001868395","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868395/000121390026100379/ea030525301ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d.bin","sha256":"28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d"}},{"id":"616a9793ae8e4094c11128912f8e43b0385e725f28d184c5fdc302bc370286da","quote":"Gross profit of offline sales to dealers decreased by 43.6%, from US$12.1 million for the six months ended June 30, 2025 to US$6.8 million for the six months ended June 30, 2026 with a relatively stable gross profit margin of around 30.7%, which was consistent with the decrease in sales revenue of offline sales to dealers.","context":"Gross profit and gross profit margin","section":"Comparison of Results of Operations for the Six Months Ended June 30, 2025 and 2026","block":89,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-100379","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-16","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001868395","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868395/000121390026100379/ea030525301ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d.bin","sha256":"28ad44bc6d1b9d89ebd73a0a014c97f0d88efbf39da9a51f27d4fcff244c4e6d"}},{"id":"d19e287b21c57aa4ca44c983818a2eb5de9706d3ba4a82af177b807b76e08ffb","quote":"Gross profit of offline sales to ODM customers increased by 73.8%, from US$7.3 million for 